/**
 * CONTRACT
 *
 * GUARANTEE: INTERFACES_TYPED — all repository interfaces use domain types
 *   from domain/types.ts and domain/status.ts. No raw DB row types appear in
 *   any method signature. make check passes with zero type errors.
 *
 * GUARANTEE: NO_DATE_OBJECTS — all timestamp parameters and return fields are
 *   Unix epoch milliseconds (number). Calendar dates (check_in, check_out) are
 *   strings. No Date objects anywhere in this file.
 *
 * GUARANTEE: CREATE_RETURNS_ID_ONLY — createWithRelations() returns
 *   { id: number } only. regCode is generated by the caller and passed in
 *   via the insert set — returning it would be redundant.
 *
 * EXPECTS: IFileStorage.getSignedUrl() is a stub for V1. R2 signed URL
 *   generation was not tested in the spike. Implementations should throw
 *   "not implemented" until the admin access sprint.
 *
 * EXPECTS: All method implementations must use parameterized prepared
 *   statements. These interfaces make no guarantee about SQL injection
 *   safety — that is the implementation's responsibility.
 *
 * FAILURE BEHAVIOR: Methods that return null (findByRegId, findValidMagicLink,
 *   IUserRepository.findById/findByEmail, IFileStorage.get) return null when
 *   not found — they do not throw. IDocumentRepository.findByRegistration
 *   returns [] when none found. All other failures propagate as thrown errors.
 */

